<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned all three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 2.599 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    349 days   20.90 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   20.81 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   19.89 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    800 million     34 days   19.91 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     17 days   19.00 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     13 days   19.49 pct</p>
<p>    149 million	3 days   19.00 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
